<title>GERMANY: D.Telekom details U.S. GAAP results.</title>
<headline>D.Telekom details U.S. GAAP results.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Telekom AG, set to list shares on international stock exchanges next month, on Friday gave the following details on net income in the first six months of 1996 and for the full year in 1995 according to U.S. generally accepted accounting principles (GAAP).</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>SIX MONTHS TO JUNE 30, 1996 vs 1995:</p>
<p>    Group net income (already reported)  500     vs 3,600</p>
<p>FULL YEAR 1995 vs 1994:</p>
<p>    Group net income			   6,460   vs 7,954</p>
<p>    Shareholders' equity (on Dec 31)     30,372  vs 24,103</p>
<p>Net income per share/ADS: (marks)</p>
<p>    Before extraordinary losses	    3.26    vs 3.92</p>
<p>    Extraordinary losses		     0.08    vs nil</p>
<p>    Net income per share/ADS		 3.18    vs 3.92</p>
<p>NOTE - All figures are from Deutsche Telekom's preliminary sales prospectus. The 1995 figures have not been adjusted for tax payments, which the company paid in 1996 for the first time.</p>
<p>-- William Boston, Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097-150</p>
